      "questionType": "FillBlank",
      "questionText": "<p><strong>Complete the text, using the words given. You may need to change the form of the words.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/images/exams/x11-min_5514d092.jpg\" alt width=\"400\"></strong></p>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.469%; height: 75px;\" border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 24.9727%; text-align: center;\"><strong>different</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 24.9727%; text-align: center;\"><strong>land</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 24.9727%; text-align: center;\"><strong>lack</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 24.8339%; text-align: center;\"><strong>inner</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 24.9727%; text-align: center;\"><strong>condition</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 24.9727%; text-align: center;\"><strong>surround</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 24.9727%; text-align: center;\"><strong>crash</strong></td>\n<td style=\"width: 24.8339%; text-align: center;\"><strong>galaxy</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br>Scientists believe that life may exist on other planets in our <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>18.1</label><input id='fbo-902202-0' class='ms fillblank-option-18' index='0' name='fbo-902202-0' type='text' size='7' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-902202-0' /></span></strong>, but the right <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>18.2</label><input id='fbo-902202-1' class='ms fillblank-option-18' index='1' name='fbo-902202-1' type='text' size='13' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-902202-1' /></span></strong> are necessary. A planet&#8217;s climate&nbsp;must be stable, and it cannot <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>18.3</label><input id='fbo-902202-2' class='ms fillblank-option-18' index='2' name='fbo-902202-2' type='text' size='8' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-902202-2' /></span></strong> essential elements like water and oxygen. Many exoplanets are <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>18.4</label><input id='fbo-902202-3' class='ms fillblank-option-18' index='3' name='fbo-902202-3' type='text' size='11' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-902202-3' /></span></strong> from Earth, with extreme temperatures and toxic atmospheres. Some <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>18.5</label><input id='fbo-902202-4' class='ms fillblank-option-18' index='4' name='fbo-902202-4' type='text' size='9' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-902202-4' /></span></strong> planets in other solar systems may have rocky surfaces where spacecraft could <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>18.6</label><input id='fbo-902202-5' class='ms fillblank-option-18' index='5' name='fbo-902202-5' type='text' size='6' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-902202-5' /></span></strong> safely. However, dangerous asteroids could <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>18.7</label><input id='fbo-902202-6' class='ms fillblank-option-18' index='6' name='fbo-902202-6' type='text' size='6' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-902202-6' /></span></strong> into them, which makes life difficult. Thick clouds of gas often <strong><span class='fillblank-option'><label>18.8</label><input id='fbo-902202-7' class='ms fillblank-option-18' index='7' name='fbo-902202-7' type='text' size='10' autocomplete='off' data-testid='fillblank-input-902202-7' /></span></strong> gas giants, preventing humans from exploring their surfaces. Finding a habitable planet remains a challenge, but scientists continue searching for new possibilities.</p>",
